# Build context of the user image (docker build -f infra/user/Dockerfile .).
# Allowlist: the manifests and the lockfile, the sources of this app and of the shared packages, and its files of infra/.
# Nothing of the admin app but its manifest (the lockfile lists it). Neither node_modules nor build output nor .env
# reach the build: dependencies are installed from the lockfile inside the image.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!infra/security-headers.conf
!apps/*/package.json
!infra/user/nginx.conf.template
!apps/user/tsconfig.json
!apps/user/vite.config.ts
!apps/user/src/
!packages/*/package.json
!packages/*/tsconfig.json
!packages/*/src/

# Inside the allowed directories
**/*.test.ts
**/.DS_Store
